A||||19||Gokart||What did I do to my headlights?||||9||
Z||000000||Gokart||07-13-2000||05:43 PM||||Washed my GT today and noticed how dirty the headlights were. Wet brushed them with soapy water then blasted them with the hose and now they won't go down <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> Checked the fuses...all good. Then replaced the light on/off switch from my parts car...no luck. The lights come on but did I kill BOTH headlight motors if they got wet? Tia for help!<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||AL||07-13-2000||08:12 PM||||the ralays got water in them disconnect them and dry them off and install and it should work, mine did the same thing, turn your lights on and move the relays a little sqweeze them and you will see that they will work.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||07-13-2000||08:22 PM||||Thanks Al! Kind of dark out now so hopefully the relays will dry by morning...if not I know what to do before I go to work <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
Z||000003||TOM||07-14-2000||12:54 AM||||I know, Buy my kit, lose the relays, and be the talk of the town.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||07-14-2000||06:40 AM||||Hey Tom, I thought your kit was to upgrade the lights to an 87/88!? My GT is an 87. Would your kit make them maitenence free! Maybe we'll work something out with that manifold you'll need when I do the swap!<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||07-14-2000||07:39 AM||||It's a no go  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Dried out what I think was the relay. Theres actually only one right? I took apart the black box mounted by the drivers side headlight and dried it with a lawn blower, put it back together and they still stay up. Is this the relay? Did I fry it for good with too much water? I also find it strange that the chime does not sound when I leave the lights on after I shut the car off? Is the chime operated by the relay as well or could it be a fuse after all?<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT<p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 07-14-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000006||Gokart||07-14-2000||08:49 PM||||I'm home from work and their STILL up! It was very hot today and I figure everything should've dried out. Can someone tell me if it was the relay that I dried out with a lawn blower this morning? Is there only one? It was mounted forward of the drivers side headlight and didn't see the same thing mounted on the passengers side.<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||8
Z||000007||StuGood||07-14-2000||09:33 PM||||I know you said earlier that you checked all the fuses, but please first re-check your 20-amp parking/tail fuse.  If blown, try replacing it.  If it immediately blows again, track down and repair whatever it is that's shorting out.<P>Naturally, since the whole thing started with washing the headlights, you'd want to begin by looking there - the parking light sockets and wiring.<P>You'll get it fixed, I'm sure     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> !  In the meantime, be glad the motors failed with the headlights UP     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> ! <BR><p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-17-2000).]||||reg||2
Z||000008||Gokart||07-14-2000||09:49 PM||||Thanks Stu! I was hoping I wasn't going to reply to my own post again for a 4th consecutive time <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif"> Will get started on those relays first thing in the morn.<P>------------------<BR> Marc                     87GT||||reg||14
Z||000009||StuGood||07-14-2000||10:12 PM||||Well, I really blew it this time (no fuse pun intended)...<P>If we are talking about an original-equipment 1987 GT, you don't HAVE the 3 relays.  Your car has an electronic controller in the LHS fender which drives the headlight motors.  The relay you found doesn't even talk to the headlight motors.  <P>Sorry about that. Think I got on the wrong track when someone posted earlier about checking relays.    <P>If I ever learn to read, I could be dangerous  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> !<P>But - ! The fact that the warning chime doesn't come on, still points to the 20-amp tail  fuse.  If parking lights don't come on, you know that's it.<P>Good Luck, and you can call me:<BR> -StuPID   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">     ||||reg||9
Z||000010||Patrick||07-15-2000||03:06 AM||||<BR>Geez Marc, now you've got me worrying about driving the Fiero at night in the rain. That would rule out only about 300 days of the year here in Vancouver... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||SCCA FIERO||07-15-2000||04:41 AM||||I thought Canadian's weren't allowed to drive at night while raining anyway.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>J/K Patrick<P>------------------<BR>-Chris <BR>88 Fiero Coupe<BR>V6 Fastback||||reg||12
Z||000012||Patrick||07-15-2000||05:23 AM||||<BR>Judging by how "new" Canadians drive in broad daylight on dry roads, that might not be such a bad idea... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000013||Gokart||07-15-2000||06:29 AM||||Yeah, now that I think of it this did happen a few other times to me last winter and I thought they might have just froze momentarily but it was also raining as well. I must have an exposed wire somewhere. Thanks for your correction Stu and I haven't gotten out there yet. I'll check that fuse again and for all your help I'd call you StuPendous <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 07-15-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000014||theogre||07-15-2000||02:04 PM||||It's posible but unlikely the motor control box is bad. I'd trace all the wiring first, making sure it's clean and tight. I'd start with trying another light switch on the dash after that. There's almost nothing to the 87+ system.<P>If you don't have another switch. try jumpering the terminals on the harness connector. Jumper the red OR orange wire to the white one acording to the diagram I have. (red goes to a fuse link. Orange goes to a 20A fuse in the pannel.) That should drop the lights if the switch is bad. (The yellow wire should raise them)<P>For reference, the relay by the left headlight is for the radiator fan.||||reg||1
Z||000015||286SE'S||07-17-2000||03:04 PM||||Does the 80's Firebird use the same headlight  controller? Where is it located in them? I have heard that the motors are the same as 87-88 Fieros. There are lots of Firebirds at the junk yard I go to and they sell the "relay' for $1.95<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||StuGood||07-17-2000||03:14 PM||||1986-earlier Fieros and Firebirds have the relay system.  1987-later Fieros and Firebirds have the electronic contoller.  <P>Firebird controller is mounted on a bracket on the firewall, near the brake master cylinder.  It is a more-or-less flat, 4" (or so) black plastic square, with raised letters that spell "GUIDE."  (Sorry -  didn't mean to shout  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  ) <P>$2 for the controller would be one <B>heck </B> of a deal, unless the proprietor of the salvage yard thinks it's just a piece of plastic.    ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Seanh||07-17-2000||06:12 PM||||Hey, I was reading about how they changed the headlight system on the 87+ Fiero. I have an 86GT. I am putting new headlights in that are diamond back lights, not exactly HID's, but they mount permently and you only replace the bulb. The bulbs just fit right into the headlight sockets. I am having a grounding problem with my passenger side light, and I am suspenting there is somthing wrong with the system. So.....I have alot of free time, and I have decided to redo the entire headlight wiring setup, relays and all. But I was reading about the later models with a different setup. Does anyone think I should just upgrade to the 87+ setup since I am redoing the whole thing anyway? Is it more advanced? or just eaiser to hook up. (I hope) This relay system looks more complicated anyway. Thanks<P>BTW, would I have to get new motors from an 87+, or will the 87+ controller hook up to 86 motors fine?<P>Sean Heberly<BR>sean@kdsi.net<BR>Silver 86GT<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 07-17-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000018||Taijiguy||07-17-2000||09:45 PM||||I'm questioning the fuse suggestion. All the electrical drawings I've seen show a fusible link as the protection for the headlight motors. The link is located back by that big terminal block next to the battery. Might check to see if it's not shot.<P>Taiji||||reg||1
Z||000019||StuGood||07-17-2000||10:52 PM||||Taijiguy:  I suggested checking the fuse first, because the it's easy to check, and  because it + light switch provide the "down" signal to the controller, through the white wire.  "Easy stuff first, as long as it's cheap" is my philosophy when it comes to troubleshooting.<P>Ogre's suggestion - checking all the wiring and connections first, makes the most sense, though, especially in light of the Gokart's later post that indicated a recurring, intermittent, "no go down" symptom.  And it's even cheaper!  That includes checking the fusible links, as you point out.  I always suggest checking fuses first, because it's less work, and I have big holdings in the fuse companies   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.  (J/K)<P>Seanh: I can recommend the upgrade to the later, electronic controller ('87+ )system.  It seems to work better, in every respect I can think of.  You <B>can</B> modify the old-style motors and make them work with the electronic controller, like I did on my 1986 SE, but it was actual <B>work</B>; something I normally avoid.  No, they do <B>not</B> hook up to the '87+ system without modification.  I recommend you get the '87+ motors to go with the controller.  If possible, get the entire front harness from an '87+ Fiero. <P>Oops   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  almost fell off the soap box   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> .  Time for Stu to shut up   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.       <P>      <p>[This message has been edited by StuGood (edited 07-17-2000).]||||reg||1
